# SFT execution status v0.78

2026-09-12. Fresh Linux CPU qualification publication/run preparation is complete
locally. No commit, push, acquisition or native attempt was started. Gate 5 is
still incomplete; the next boundary is a new explicitly approved CPU-only job.

## Completed in this stage

The new acquisition script uses at most four sequential HTTP responses: prior
successful guardian job metadata, exact accepted-software artifact metadata,
one signed-URL redirect and one credential-free software ZIP GET. The original
accepted ZIP/tar hashes are unchanged. Expired, missing, changed or failed input
stops without rebuilding, substituting or retrying. The old diagnostic artifact
and exhausted old preparer are not replayed.

A fresh private workflow binds the harness, supervisor, acquirer and verifier
hashes before acquisition. It checks the 57-file source admission and runs 133
pure preflight tests without installing dependencies. The native command uses
the supervisor's exact empty-plus-three-variable environment and signals only
the harness pidfd, never a guardian/process group.

The full aggregate verifier checks acquisition, supervisor, ordered cases,
nested worker receipts, source/software pins, rootfs/add-on counts, owned
cleanup and input retirement. It requires zero unexpected adopted children.
Upload is limited to four explicitly named, bounded aggregate JSON files.
Failed or partial evidence is never overwritten to manufacture a success.

Local final verification: 1,179 source/double tests pass on Python 3.11.15,
3.13.7 and 3.14.6, with no failures/skips. This includes 52 new tests.
Ruff E,F,I,B,UP / py311 / line100 passes on five new Python files; YAML parses
as one job/seven steps. The previous 100 tiny-CPU tests remain in frozen v0.77
evidence; they were not rerun or counted again in this stage.

The exact 133 future preflight tests also pass under an absolute-path
publication dependency check: 70 repository files were observed, with no
unpublished absolute-path dependency, network/native call or ML import.
Python's open audit event omits dir_fd; 698 relative/dirfd fixture opens are
explicitly unresolved. Two initial overly conservative instrumentation runs
interfered with generated-rootfs operations; only the instrumentation was
corrected. This check is not a universal dynamic-closure or native OS proof.

